@* Three explicit theme buttons — Light / Dark / Colorblind-safe. Deliberately no
   Blazor state or IJSRuntime here: onclick (lowercase, not @onclick) is a raw HTML
   attribute Blazor passes straight through, so clicking calls the global
   window.faSetTheme(...) from js/theme.js directly, client-side only. Which button
   looks "active" is also handled by that script (see markActive there), not by
   anything this component tracks — there's nothing here for a re-render to get
   out of sync with. *@

<div class="fa-theme-switcher" role="group" aria-label="Theme">
    <button type="button" class="fa-theme-btn" data-theme-btn="light" title="Light theme"
            aria-pressed="false" onclick="faSetTheme('light')">
        <FaIcon Name="FaIconName.Sun" Color="FaIconColor.White" Size="16" Title="Light theme" />
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="fa-theme-btn" data-theme-btn="dark" title="Dark theme"
            aria-pressed="false" onclick="faSetTheme('dark')">
        <FaIcon Name="FaIconName.Moon" Color="FaIconColor.White" Size="16" Title="Dark theme" />
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="fa-theme-btn" data-theme-btn="colorblind" title="Colorblind-safe theme"
            aria-pressed="false" onclick="faSetTheme('colorblind')">
        <FaIcon Name="FaIconName.Eye" Color="FaIconColor.White" Size="16" Title="Colorblind-safe theme" />
    </button>
</div>
